<main id="main" class="container about-page"><p class="eyebrow">A STUDENT PROJECT WITH LOCAL ROOTS</p><h1>A space built<br>on <em>possibility.</em></h1><p class="lead">Salone Studio is an independent learning-portal concept for the Django Girls community in Sierra Leone.</p><div class="about-columns"><section><h2>The inspiration</h2><p>Django Girls is a programming community that makes technology more approachable for women. Its official Freetown page documents a local workshop held in October 2017. This project draws on that local connection without presenting a new workshop or official service.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://djangogirls.org/de/freetown1/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the Freetown community page <?= icon('arrow') ?></a><h2>What this studio does</h2><p>Create an account, log in securely, explore a four-lesson web learning path, and save your progress. Your dashboard shows your own goal and recent activity. The portal is implemented in PHP as part of Web Programming Assignment 1.</p></section><section><h2>Design &amp; credits</h2><p>The Django Girls logo comes from the organisation’s official resources repository. Warm orange, paper tones, and hand-drawn accents reference that identity. The Freetown-inspired illustration, page layout, and lesson content were created for this project.</p><p>No theme, UI framework, or third-party plugin is used. Links on the resource shelf point to their respective official publishers.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/DjangoGirls/resources" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official logo resources <?= icon('arrow') ?></a><h2>Account privacy</h2><p>This prototype stores your name, email, password hash, learning goal, progress, and account activity in the local XAMPP MySQL database. It uses a necessary session cookie. There are no analytics or advertising cookies.</p></section></div><div class="project-notice"><h2>Independent prototype</h2><p>This is a student project, not an official Django Girls website. It does not enrol people in a real event or issue qualifications. Lesson completion records a simple knowledge check, not a certification. Logo ownership remains with Django Girls; external reuse must follow the organisation’s asset permission requirements.</p></div><a class="button" href="<?= $user ? 'dashboard.php' : 'signup.php' ?>"><?= $user ? 'Return to my workspace' : 'Begin your journey' ?> <?= icon('arrow') ?></a></main><?php render_footer(); ?>
